<para id="RM00000060900ZX" category="C" type-id="3009U" name-id="442OD-00" from="200612">
<dtccode>C0200/31</dtccode>
<dtcname>Speed Sensor FR System Malfunction</dtcname>
<dtccode>C0205/32</dtccode>
<dtcname>Speed Sensor FL System Malfunction</dtcname>
<dtccode>C0210/33</dtccode>
<dtcname>Speed Sensor RR System Malfunction</dtcname>
<dtccode>C0215/34</dtccode>
<dtcname>Speed Sensor RL System Malfunction</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM00000060900ZX_05" type-id="33" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00007LQ00000">
<name>Function Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>The speed sensors detect the wheel speeds and send signals to the skid control computer. These signals are used for ABS control.</ptxt>
<ptxt>The speed sensor generates vehicle speed pulses by detecting changes in the magnetic field of a magnetic rotor with N/S poles evenly distributed around its circumference.</ptxt>
<ptxt>From these vehicle speed pulses, the skid control computer detects each wheel speed.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="C121324J02" width="7.106578999in" height="4.7836529in"/>
</figure>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.70in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.69in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="2.69in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC No.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Detection Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Output Related Items</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>C0200/31</ptxt>
<ptxt>C0205/32</ptxt>
<ptxt>C0210/33</ptxt>
<ptxt>C0215/34</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>At a vehicle speed of 10km/h or more, an open or short in the speed sensor signal circuit continues for 1 seconds or more</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When an open in the sensor signal of the malfunctioning wheel occurs 255 times or more</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>An open in the speed sensor signal circuit continues for 0.5 seconds or more</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When IG1 terminal voltage is 9.5 V or higher and the sensor power source voltage remains low for 0.5 seconds or more</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Open or short in speed sensor</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Speed sensor improperly installed or abnormal clearance with sensor rotor</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Open or short in wire harness</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Poor connector contact pressure, terminal deformation or corrosion</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Foreign matter adhering to speed sensor</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Sensor rotor malfunction (foreign matter adhesion, damage)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Wiring resistance of speed sensor circuit</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Actuator assembly</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
